   "stem": {
      "text": "A ladder 15 meters long leans against a vertical wall. The bottom of the ladder slides away from the wall along level ground at a constant rate of 6 meters per second. At the instant when the bottom of the ladder is 12 meters from the wall, find the rate of change of the height of the top of the ladder. Give an exact answer with units.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -8,
      "units": "meters per second"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "With x the distance from the wall to the bottom and y the height of the top, \\( x^{2} + y^{2} = 225 \\).",
         "rule_named": "relating equation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At the instant x = 12, so \\( y = \\sqrt{225 - 144} = 9 \\).",
         "mathjson": 9,
         "rule_named": "missing instantaneous value from the relating equation"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Differentiate with respect to time: \\( 2x\\frac{dx}{dt} + 2y\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0 \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Substitute x = 12, y = 9 and \\( \\frac{dx}{dt} = 6 \\): \\( \\frac{dy}{dt} = -\\frac{x}{y}\\frac{dx}{dt} = -8 \\), negative because the top slides down.",
         "mathjson": -8,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "substitute after differentiating"
      }
   ],
